<title>GERMANY: Metro sells furniture retail unit.</title>
<headline>Metro sells furniture retail unit.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German retail concern Metro AG said on Tuesday it would sell furniture retailer Moebel Unger GmbH to an investment group for 190 million marks.</p>
<p>The sale would be effective July 1 and Metro would assume Moebel Unger's operating losses in the first half of the year, the company said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Moebel Unger had 1996 gross sales of 1.23 billion marks, although resturcturing charges left it with &quot;clear losses,&quot; Metro said.</p>
<p>The unit employed 4,140 workers and operated 63 furniture stores last year.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
